  "notes": "Example only. Cylindrical hull 2.2 m x 0.32 m. Inertia: solid cylinder. Drag: 0.5*rho*Cd*A with Cd 0.3 axial, 1.0 cross-flow. Added mass: 10% axial, rho*pi*r^2*L cross-flow. Added inertia: the cross-flow strips about the centre, A*a^2/3 (a = half length). Slightly positively buoyant (about 5 N net in 1025 kg/m3 water) so it surfaces if power is lost. Cruciform tail: two rudders and two hydroplanes, 0.1 m2 each, lift slope 2.2/rad (pair aspect ratio about 1.6, Helmbold), 25 deg deflection; the area includes an allowance for hull lift, which the simplified model does not compute, so the hull is directionally stable against its Munk moment."
